# Reuse Existing Functionality

Do not add a parallel implementation of something the codebase already does. Search first, then reuse or extend.

## Must do

- Before a new helper, query, mapper, or UI block, search the repo for the same job (same aggregation, type mapping, filter, status, payload shape).
- Prefer **reuse as-is**, then **reuse in part** (shared helper, extra column/parameter), then last: a new path.
- When extending, list callers and mismatches; run tests for those callers.
- Add a similar new function only when changing the old one would break a caller that needs different semantics — and say why reuse is impossible.

```text
❌ BAD: Copy an existing mapper/aggregation into a second path with new labels.
✅ GOOD: Extend the existing source of truth; keep one definition of the business result.

❌ BAD: Fork a shared details/status component for a new variant with hard-coded names.
✅ GOOD: Reuse the shared component; add only what the new variant uniquely needs.
```
